<h2>Asobi 0.2 (build 473)</h2>
<p><b>Quieter progress, and a File menu you can read.</b></p>
<ul>
<li><b>Fixed: background work announced itself as an "Error".</b> Optimising progress, "playlist sorted", "deleted 1 stand-in" — all of it came up as a modal error dialog, and progress put one up on every update. Progress now sits in the header as a thin bar with a percentage, and one-off confirmations appear as a small line at the bottom of the picture that fades on its own. The Error alert is for actual errors again.</li>
<li><b>The File menu is grouped instead of a twenty-item list.</b> Bringing work in, optimized media, and exporting each collapse into their own submenu; Save, Export Frame Grab and Share to Web stay where your hand already goes. Every shortcut is unchanged.</li>
<li><b>The floating playlist fills its window</b>, so widening it shows more of each shot name — and <b>the playlist can be sorted</b> by name, date or duration, with version groups kept together.</li>
</ul>
]]></description>
